NAME
       e2label - show or change the label of an ext2/3/4 file system

SYNOPSIS
       e2label DEVICE [NEW-LABEL]

DESCRIPTION
       With only DEVICE, e2label prints the file system's label. With
       NEW-LABEL it sets the label (up to 16 characters). A label lets
       /etc/fstab name the file system as LABEL=NAME instead of by device
       or UUID. tune2fs -L does the same.

       For xfs use xfs_admin -L, for vfat fatlabel.

EXAMPLES
           e2label /dev/vdb1 BACKUP
           echo "LABEL=BACKUP /backup ext4 defaults 0 0" >> /etc/fstab

SEE ALSO
       tune2fs(8), blkid(8), xfs_admin(8), fatlabel(8)
